## Ash on the tongue

::bg{location="hearth" time="night"}
::music{action="start" mood="hearth" volume="down"}
@narrator{code="0010"}: Wren wakes on warm stone with ash in her mouth and no memory of lying down.
@narrator{code="0020"}: Above her, the Stair goes up into the dark, one step at a time, forever.
::use{component="hearthFire" flare="high"}
::auto{character="maud" anchor="center" action="fadeInUp"}
@maud{code="0010" emotion="warm"}: There you are. Don't sit up too fast — the first time, everyone throws up.
@wren{code="0010"}: Where is this?
@maud{code="0020" emotion="wry"}: The bottom. The Hearth. The only warm place between here and the top.
@maud{code="0030"}: You'll climb. You'll fall. You'll wake up right where you're lying now, and I'll have the kettle on.

<branch id="firstWords" prompt="Maud holds out a chipped cup.">
  <choice id="take" label="Take the cup">
    ::set{user.bond.maud += 1}
    @maud{code="0040" emotion="fond"}: Good. Manners survive the ash. That's a start.
  </choice>
  <choice id="refuse" label="I'm not staying.">
    @maud{code="0050" emotion="wry"}: Nobody is, love. That's rather the point of the Stair.
  </choice>
</branch>

@maud{code="0060"}: Go on, then. The smith is by the anvil and the quiet one is by the water. Mind them both.
